# =============================================================
# Asset protection — DO NOT REMOVE LINES WITHOUT REVIEW
# This repo is public. Anything that lands in git history is
# forensically recoverable forever, even after deletion.
# =============================================================

# --- Licensed/paid asset folders (defense layer 1: explicit) ---
assets/
assetszipped/

# --- LimeZu (PAID, non-redistributable) — must NEVER be committed ---
# LimeZu art is not free to redistribute, so it can't live in a public repo.
# The source library lives OUTSIDE the repo;
# these patterns are a name-based safety net in case a copy is ever dropped
# into the tree. PNGs aren't extension-blocked (Kenney CC0 art is allowed), so
# the only thing standing between LimeZu and a leak is matching its name.
# Bracket classes cover the common casings: Limezu / limezu / LimeZu / limeZu.
*[Ll]ime[Zz]u*

# --- Kenney bulk library — CC0, but keep the repo LEAN ---
# Kenney art is CC0 (legally hostable), but there's no reason to mirror
# Kenney's entire multi-hundred-MB catalog into a public game repo. Policy:
# commit ONLY the curated subset the game actually renders (see the allowlist
# below); keep the full source library out. These patterns block the library
# folder if it's ever dropped into the tree. Bracket classes cover casings;
# the `*Assets*` requirement means they do NOT match the curated `kenney/`
# bundle dir (which has no "Assets" in its name).
*[Kk]enney*[Aa]ssets*
*[Kk]enney [Gg]ame [Aa]ssets*

# --- What IS allowed (CC0 / first-party) ---
# game/assets/ — procedurally-generated, authored by us (bitmap fonts, UI
#   panels, wheel frames — output of tools/ scripts). First-party, safe.
# game/assets-placeholder/kenney/ — the CURATED subset of Kenney CC0 packs the
#   game renders. Intentionally COMMITTED: public-domain AND required to render.
#   Only copy the specific sheets the game uses here — never whole packs or the
#   full library. (The `assets/` and `*Kenney*Assets*` rules do NOT match this
#   path — different names — so it stays tracked. Do not "fix" that.)
!game/assets/
!game/assets/**

# --- Archive & executable files (defense layer 2: extensions) ---
# Catches any new asset zip dropped anywhere, plus installers/launchers.
# The repo ships pure HTML/CSS/JS; no legitimate need to commit these.
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.exe
*.msi
*.dmg

# --- Source-art files (defense layer 3: art extensions) ---
# Asset packs often include editable source files alongside PNGs.
# These are higher-value than exported sprites and must not leak.
*.psd
*.aseprite
*.ase
*.xcf
*.kra
*.clip

# --- Regenerable dev artifacts (keep the repo lean) ---
# Labeled coord-picking contact sheets are large Kenney-derived montages,
# not needed at runtime, and reproducible in seconds via
# tools/gen_contact_sheet.py. Commit the script, not its output. Also catch
# the underscore-prefixed scratch crops agents leave behind.
tools/contact_*.png
tools/_*.png

# --- Brainstorm / design scratch (visual companion) ---
# Throwaway mockup HTML I serve through the dev server while designing a
# feature, plus any superpowers brainstorm session state. Pure scratch —
# never part of the shipped game. Keep it untracked.
.superpowers/
game/_design-*.html
game/_ui-preview*

# --- Local dev config & collaborator files (not for the public repo) ---
# .claude/launch.json is a machine-specific dev-server launch path.
# *-TheDangerrZone* are a collaborator's parallel variants, maintained
# locally and not ours to publish.
.claude/launch.json
*-TheDangerrZone*

# --- OS / editor housekeeping ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
